{"tool_name":"mrbayes","contents":["biocontainers","bioschemas","debian","biotools","bioconda","oeb"],"fetched_metadata":{"bioconda":{"name":"mrbayes","version":"3.2.7","home":"https://github.com/NBISweden/MrBayes","documentation":"https://nbisweden.github.io/MrBayes/","license":"GPL-3.0-or-later","summary":"Bayesian Inference of Phylogeny","identifiers":["biotools:mrbayes"],"description":"MrBayes is a program for Bayesian inference and model choice across a wide\nrange of phylogenetic and evolutionary models. MrBayes uses Markov chain\nMonte Carlo (MCMC) methods to estimate the posterior distribution of model\nparameters.\n","license_file":"COPYING","build":{"number":7,"run_exports":[null]},"requirements":{"build":[null,"make"],"host":["readline","openmpi","beagle-lib <4","ncurses"],"run":["readline","openmpi","beagle-lib <4","ncurses"]},"source_url":"https://github.com/NBISweden/MrBayes/archive/v3.2.7.tar.gz","test":{"commands":["echo Version | mb","echo Version | mpirun -mca plm_rsh_agent true --allow-run-as-root mb-mpi"]}},"biocontainers":{"name":"mrbayes","identifiers":["biotools:mrbayes","doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/17.8.754"],"license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Bayesian inference of phylogeny","home_url":"https://github.com/NBISweden/MrBayes","keywords":["Bayes Theorem","Computational Biology","Markov Chains","Phylogeny","Phylogenetics","Genetics"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":4885},"biotools":{"id":"mrbayes","home":"http://nbisweden.github.io/MrBayes/","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Program for Bayesian inference and model choice across a wide range of phylogenetic and evolutionary models. It uses Markov chain Monte Carlo (MCMC) methods to estimate the posterior distribution of model parameters.","addition_date":"2016-04-21T06:14:09Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T14:33:52.385956Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"version":["3.2.6"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:mrbayes","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"name":"Dept. of Biodiversity Informatics at the Swedish Museum of Natural History","typeEntity":"Institute","typeRole":["Provider"]},{"name":"Fredrik Ronquist","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Developer"]},{"name":"NIH","typeEntity":"Funding agency","typeRole":["Contributor"]},{"name":"NSF","typeEntity":"Funding agency","typeRole":["Contributor"]},{"name":"Vetenskapsr\u00e5det","typeEntity":"Funding agency","typeRole":["Contributor"]},{"name":"icm.uu.se","typeEntity":"Institute","typeRole":["Provider"]},{"name":"Bret Larget","typeRole":["Contributor"]},{"name":"Chi Zhang","typeRole":["Contributor"]},{"name":"Donald Simon","typeRole":["Contributor"]},{"name":"John Huelsenbeck","typeRole":["Contributor"]},{"name":"Maxim Teslenko","typeRole":["Contributor"]},{"name":"Paul van der Mark","typeRole":["Contributor"]},{"typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"http://nbisweden.github.io/MrBayes/"}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://nbisweden.github.io/MrBayes/"},{"type":["Terms of use"],"url":"https://github.com/NBISweden/MrBayes/blob/develop/COPYING"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["EngyNasr","sergitobara"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Phylogenetic tree generation (maximum likelihood and Bayesian methods)","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0547"}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"MrBayes","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"andreas.kahari@icm.uu.se","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/sysbio/sys029","metadata":{"abstract":"Since its introduction in 2001, MrBayes has grown in popularity as a software package for Bayesian phylogenetic inference using Markov chain Monte Carlo (MCMC) methods. With this note, we announce the release of version 3.2, a major upgrade to the latest official release presented in 2003. The new version provides convergence diagnostics and allows multiple analyses to be run in parallel with convergence progress monitored on the fly. The introduction of new proposals and automatic optimization of tuning parameters has improved convergence for many problems. The new version also sports significantly faster likelihood calculations through streaming single-instruction-multiple-data extensions (SSE) and support of the BEAGLE library, allowing likelihood calculations to be delegated to graphics processing units (GPUs) on compatible hardware. Speedup factors range from around 2 with SSE code to more than 50 with BEAGLE for codon problems. Checkpointing across all models allows long runs to be completed even when an analysis is prematurely terminated. New models include relaxed clocks, dating, model averaging across time-reversible substitution models, and support for hard, negative, and partial (backbone) tree constraints. Inference of species trees from gene trees is supported by full incorporation of the Bayesian estimation of species trees (BEST) algorithms. Marginal model likelihoods for Bayes factor tests can be estimated accurately across the entire model space using the stepping stone method. The new version provides more output options than previously, including samples of ancestral states, site rates, site dN/dS rations, branch rates, and node dates. A wide range of statistics on tree parameters can also be output for visualization in FigTree and compatible software. \u00a9 2012 The Author(s).","authors":[{"name":"Ayres D.L."},{"name":"Darling A."},{"name":"Hohna S."},{"name":"Huelsenbeck J.P."},{"name":"Larget B."},{"name":"Liu L."},{"name":"Ronquist F."},{"name":"Suchard M.A."},{"name":"Teslenko M."},{"name":"Van Der Mark P."}],"citationCount":21986,"date":"2012-05-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Systematic Biology","title":"Mrbayes 3.2: Efficient bayesian phylogenetic inference and model choice across a large model space"},"pmcid":"PMC3329765","pmid":"22357727","version":"3.2"},{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/17.8.754","metadata":{"abstract":"Summary: The program MRBAYES performs Bayesian inference of phylogeny using a variant of Markov chain Monte Carlo.","authors":[{"name":"Huelsenbeck J.P."},{"name":"Ronquist F."}],"citationCount":20446,"date":"2001-01-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"MRBAYES: Bayesian inference of phylogenetic trees"},"pmid":"11524383","version":"3"},{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btg180","metadata":{"abstract":"Summary: MrBayes 3 performs Bayesian phylogenetic analysis combining information from different data partitions or subsets evolving under different stochastic evolutionary models. This allows the user to analyze heterogeneous data sets consisting of different data types - e.g. morphological, nucleotide, and protein - and to explore a wide variety of structured models mixing partition-unique and shared parameters. The program employs MPI to parallelize Metropolis coupling on Macintosh or UNIX clusters.","authors":[{"name":"Huelsenbeck J.P."},{"name":"Ronquist F."}],"citationCount":26954,"date":"2003-08-12T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"MrBayes 3: Bayesian phylogenetic inference under mixed models"},"pmid":"12912839","version":"3"}],"topic":[{"term":"Phylogenetics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3293"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"MrBayes","home":"https://bio.tools/mrbayes","license":"GPL-3.0","version":"3.2.6","summary":"Program for Bayesian inference and model choice across a wide range of phylogenetic and evolutionary models. It uses Markov chain Monte Carlo (MCMC) methods to estimate the posterior distribution of model parameters.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:mrbayes:3.2.6/cmd/nbisweden.github.io","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":true,"registration":false},"packages":true,"source_packages":true,"sourcecode":{"free":true,"interpreted":false,"license":true,"public":true,"readme":true,"repository":{"anonymous":true,"online":true}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"docum